Q: You're trying to write a program that will help you get your car out of the mud. The program should print the following:
- If you have a tow rope: "I can pull the car out!"
- If you don't have a tow rope: "I need a tow rope to pull the car out!"
- If you don't know if you have a tow rope: "I don't know if I have a tow rope."

Write the code in C++:
A: #include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
bool hasTowRope = false;

if (hasTowRope) {
cout << "I can pull the car out!" << endl;
} else {
cout << "I need a tow rope to pull the car out!" << endl;
}

return 0;
}
